{"id":"ba7caadd24f5c047a8cd4fc8f18fc03a503d982e","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/lucene","sha":"ba7caadd24f5c047a8cd4fc8f18fc03a503d982e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"lucene/CHANGES.txt","lines":["@@ -79,6 +79,10 @@ API Changes"," * GITHUB#16741: Lower the minimum supported major version from 10 to 9. Indexes created with 9.x","   remain fully supported in Lucene 11, no reindexing required. (Luca Cavanna)"," ","+* GITHUB#17084: IntervalsSource has a new abstract method maxExtent(), the counterpart of","+  minExtent(). Custom IntervalsSource implementations must implement it; return Integer.MAX_VALUE","+  if the width of the intervals is not bounded. (Alan Woodward)","+"," * GITHUB#14399: Sort pruning decisions are now entirely made through the Pruning","   enum.  The various different locations that made these decisions are consolidated","   into FieldValueHitQueue, and early termination through examining index sorts is","@@ -330,6 +334,10 @@ Improvements"," "," Optimizations"," ---------------------","+* GITHUB#17084: Unordered, ordered and maxgaps intervals over a disjunction no longer expand","+  alternatives that always match the same fixed width (such as single terms, wildcards and","+  phrases of equal length) into a cross product of separate sources. (Alan Woodward)","+"," * GITHUB#16145: Bound the prefetch backoff in MemorySegmentIndexInput. The gap between page-cache probes used to","   grow without limit, so under memory pressure prefetch effectively stopped working. A file now probes on every","   prefetch call until 1024 consecutive hits, then every 256th call; a miss goes back to probing on every call."],"additions":8,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lucene/MIGRATE.md","lines":["@@ -28,6 +28,18 @@ with `VisitedSet.create(expectedVisitedNodes, graphSize)`."," "," ## Migration from Lucene 10.x to Lucene 11.0"," ","+### IntervalsSource.maxExtent() is abstract (GITHUB#17084)","+","+`IntervalsSource` has a new abstract method `maxExtent()`, the counterpart of `minExtent()`. It","+returns the largest width of any interval the source can return. Disjunctions use it to combine","+alternatives that always have the same width, which avoids expanding them into a cross product","+when they sit under an unordered, ordered or `maxgaps` source.","+","+Custom `IntervalsSource` subclasses must implement it. If the width of your intervals is not","+bounded, or you are not sure, return `Integer.MAX_VALUE`, which is always safe. Only return a","+value equal to `minExtent()` if every interval your source returns has exactly that width in","+every document, including at the start and end of a field.","+"," ### Monitor's QueryTree subclasses implement collectTerms(TermCollector) (GITHUB#16997)"," "," `QueryTree#collectTerms(TermCollector)` is now the abstract method, and"],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lucene/queries/src/java/org/apache/lucene/queries/intervals/BlockIntervalsSource.java","lines":["@@ -65,6 +65,15 @@ public int minExtent() {","     return minExtent;","   }"," ","+  @Override","+  public int maxExtent() {","+    long maxExtent = 0;","+    for (IntervalsSource subSource : subSources) {","+      maxExtent += subSource.maxExtent();","+    }","+    return (int) Math.min(maxExtent, Integer.MAX_VALUE);","+  }","+","   @Override","   public Collection<IntervalsSource> pullUpDisjunctions() {","     return Collections.singletonList(this); // Disjunctions already pulled up in build()"],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lucene/queries/src/java/org/apache/lucene/queries/intervals/ContainedByIntervalsSource.java","lines":["@@ -79,6 +79,11 @@ public int minExtent() {","     return small.minExtent();","   }"," ","+  @Override","+  public int maxExtent() {","+    return small.maxExtent();","+  }","+","   @Override","   public Collection<IntervalsSource> pullUpDisjunctions() {","     return Disjunctions.pullUp(big, s -> new ContainedByIntervalsSource(small, s));"],"additions":5,"dele